{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep","id":1490718,"title":"Electric Sheep","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-19T09:21:35-07:00","id":1490718,"title":"Electric Sheep","content":"So, I never played CtD, but have some basic understanding of the Dreaming from crossing over from other splats. My current campaign has an oneiromancer, and I had an idea for something I might need some pointers for from players / STs with a little more direct experience.<br /> <br /> Google <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepDream\" target=\"_blank\">DeepDream</a> was a project that (initially) explored the possibility of taking a look inside the black box of a neural network, which is usually something very difficult to do. They side-stepped the issue by using a network trained on image recognition and made it 'run in reverse' - I won't get into software engineering details on how that is misleading, but it suffices as a generalization.<br /> <br /> Machine Learning software has become very prominent since then; things like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Dungeon\" target=\"_blank\">AI Dungeon</a> popped up, and currently image creators like <a href=\"https://openai.com/blog/dall-e/\" target=\"_blank\">DALL-E</a> or <a href=\"https://www.midjourney.com/showcase/\" target=\"_blank\">Midjourney</a> are vogue. Commercially, Machine Learning algorithms are pretty widespread for anything that involves pattern recognition, like search and recommendation engines, the visual processing of self-driving cars, surveillance and so on.<br /> <br /> I'm avoiding calling them Artificial Intelligence because while results get more impressive, they are still a far cry from conscious. Within the WoD however, true AI already exists.<br /> <br /> My point here is, could the current state of rudimentary 'creativity' of ML together with the widespread application of the technology already be enough to affect the Dreaming? Could you imagine a 'section' of the Dreaming where those created images and stories accumulate to build a new realm? Or would it be its own thing, a Chimare separate from the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> Extrapolating from this, would the created Chimeras be different from those created by human dreamers? It's difficult not to project <a href=\"https://futurism.com/ai-nightmare-crungus\" target=\"_blank\">expectations</a> into those images, even though the neural net that created them has no idea what the images represent.<br /> <br /> Is there any official release that explores machine dreams?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T09:53:30-07:00","id":1490722,"title":"","content":"Nothing for changeling the dreaming, no. However:<br /> <br /> Mage has the Digital Web, which could be thought of as the digital equivalent of the Dreaming. <br /> <br /> Changeling the Lost has recently released for preview Kith and Kin, which includes a section on the briar net, a digital counterpart to the Hedge (Lost's counterpart to the Dreaming).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T12:05:53-07:00","id":1490726,"title":"","content":"I've always thought of the Digital Web as human ideation combined with the reflection of the physical digital infrastructure- human dreams on digital foundation, if you will. What I'm looking at is the reverse: organic dreams from digital entities. Or proto-entities, at this point. It's a point worth discussing, but I think there is a qualitative difference between the two.<br /> <br /> I unfortunately know next to nothing about CoD books, other than what I read on secondary sources. I will at least need to do some wiki browsing on the Hedge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T12:35:13-07:00","id":1490728,"title":"","content":"The upcoming lore of the traditions explains that the notion of the digital web is not necessarily as limited as previous editions have presented it as. In particular, the author of the chapter on the virtual Adepts is on record saying that in his view, every Mage potentially has access to some aspect of the digital web; and the other aspects aren't necessarily digital. There is mention of a verbena style part of the digital web that has a very organic aspect to it. And I'm sure that there are some steampunk enthusiasts who access a more mechanical portion of the digital web, something with much more of a steampunk aesthetic. I mentioned the latter because to the extent that changeling deals with technology, it typically deals with it in terms of a steampunk aesthetic.<br /> <br /> But I get what you're saying. I will also note that there is a cyber web in the middle umbra which serves as a bridge of sorts between the Middle umbra and the digital web. It would not surprise me in the least if there was something similar in the dreaming. As I said, though, the Dreaming version is more likely to have Steampunk aesthetics, with gears and clockwork automatons rather than electricity. Possibly play up how the originals Difference Engine was inspired by automated looms, and present stored data in the form of elaborate tapestries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T12:45:33-07:00","id":1490729,"title":"","content":"I would always make a distinction between the Dreaming itself and any other Dreamlands style realms in the Dream Zone. Once you start including any kind of items of human imagination in the Dreaming, you quickly have a setting that is departing from what people imagine a Fairyland to be like. I don't think you can have a game about fairies if the fairies and fairyland become unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> I think there is something &quot;real&quot; and &quot;primal&quot; about the Dreaming that does not apply to any Dream realms only fueled by human imagination and wonder. You can come up with various explanations for that.<br /> <br /> I would allow for SOME crossover in the sense that it is always possible to somehow travel other parts of reality. So if an ST wanted changelings to somehow enter the Digital Web, that's OK. The same is there was somehow a lost spirit or group of spirits from these other realms &quot;invade&quot; the Dreaming, I'd be fine with that. An ST could create good adventures for his PCs.<br /> <br /> But personally, I wouldn't want computers creating spirits or chimera that appear in the Dreaming. That's just my personal taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:39:41-07:00","id":1490743,"title":"","content":"Oh, I thought the Near Dreaming was relatively close to the mundane world and contemporary in nature, with the more fairyland-ish things deeper in? Maybe I'm working on a wrong understanding of the geography here, or using wrong nomenclature.<br /> As far as I understood it, fictional and daydream stuff has its own realms, while the Dreaming serves as general canvas for - and is created by - the mass of dreamers. That's why I was assuming that new types of dreams, regardless of who does the dreaming, would be incorporated in there.<br /> <br /> I can totally understand not wanting too much cross-over stuff disrupting the general ambience, btw. I'm coming at this from the 'outside', and maybe this thread would have been better placed in the Mage forum.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T21:26:25-07:00","id":1490755,"title":"","content":"To answer this question it is necessary to understand the nature of the Dreaming (roughly, as many details remain unanswered, obviously).<br /> <br /> And the first thing to understand is that the Dreaming is older than humanity, and the second that it is a realm of Glamour, not of literal Dreams. While dreams may manifest there, this is not the point.<br /> <br /> What the Dreaming is is the realm of stories and emotions. It is a place that gather the feelings of everything in the world that has the capacity to feel and turns it into forms following the Laws of Narratives.<br /> <br /> It is also a place of creation. It is not the Astral Umbra. When you imagine something and your imagination takes form from Glamour, it is a Chimera, but the fae aren't Chimera, and not every Chimera is formed that way. No human in the WoD thought of the Tuatha, or any of the Kiths, before the Dreaming itself spawned them. Fears of hunger and predation fueled the birth of the Redcaps, but there was no legend about Redcaps before the Dreaming made them.<br /> <br /> So none of this is how the Dreaming works. If such Chimera do exist, they exist either in the Autumn World or the Near Dreaming, because Chimera spawned by imagination are spawned near their creators. The things that spawn within the Dreaming itself derive from the nature of that place and have no connection to this world, although they <i>may</i> one day come to it and become known to mortal legend, just as the Kiths did.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Dreaming already has things that aren't related to human dreams. Among the Gallain we have already some prime examples, like the Dark-kin and the Inanimae. Pay attention to the Inanimae on that: they're <i>possibly</i> not born of the dreams about natural phenomena and physical things, but the dreams <i><b>from</b></i> natural phenomena and physical things.<br /> <br /> By the way, currently among the Inanimae there's already the Empire of Flickers, composed of Krofted Mannikins linked to televisions, computers and other broadcasts. An Inanimae linked to a Neural Network could be either a Mannikin or, possibly, a Solimond. Learning about the Inanimae will be good for you to answer this question. But while they travel to farther reaches of the Dreaming, the Inanimae do belong to the Autumn World and can't unfetter themselves permanently from it.<br /> <br /> Yes, in the end it is probable that such things already have some form of impact on the Dreaming, both because of the dreams caused by them and their own possibly-existing dreams (the Dreaming <b>can</b> react to imagination of things that don't have an actual imagination, because the Dreaming answers only to itself), but at the same time this impact exists within the terms of the Dreaming, and out there will take forms unrelated to their Autumn counterpart, forms that pertain only to the context of the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T03:33:11-07:00","id":1490775,"title":"","content":"This is interesting, because it is metaphysically rather different to how Maya is portrayed in MtA or the Dream Zone in WtA. What I gather from all of your answers is that machine dreams may be better placed in their own Realm that may be connected to the Dreaming in some way, but is separate. One really good point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> brought up is Glamour, which is something I don't believe machines are able to produce, as it requires emotion. Of course, they can <i>inspire </i>wonder in dreamers, but that's a different thing - there may be a Crungus Chimera in the Dreaming, but only as a result of people fueling the narrative.<br /> <br /> When thinking about it like that, the notion of something that could qualify as dreaming but is devoid of Glamour would probably be rather suspect to Dream denizens. Can something completely bereft of emotion be considered banal?<br /> <br /> If at some point in the future AI evolves enough to be self-aware, have emotions and all the good stuff, things may change but this is ways off.<br /> <br /> Inanimae sound like a really interesting concept, I've noticed it in discussions before. Before I dive into that it looks like I would need to get the core book and have a crash course though, to have a chance to understand what is going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T04:06:52-07:00","id":1490776,"title":"","content":"For the Inanimae, I strongly recommend getting their 1e sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T09:10:58-07:00","id":1490798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490776#post1490776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Inanimae, I strongly recommend getting their 1e sourcebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The C20 Core isn't a bad initiation, but their original sourcebook will help a lot. The Wiki does it too, if this is not an option (for some reason the people that update the Changeling pages in the wiki has the tendency to fully parse the original text, btw).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490775#post1490775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting, because it is metaphysically rather different to how Maya is portrayed in MtA or the Dream Zone in WtA. What I gather from all of your answers is that machine dreams may be better placed in their own Realm that may be connected to the Dreaming in some way, but is separate. One really good point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> brought up is Glamour, which is something I don't believe machines are able to produce, as it requires emotion. Of course, they can <i>inspire </i>wonder in dreamers, but that's a different thing - there may be a Crungus Chimera in the Dreaming, but only as a result of people fueling the narrative.<br /> <br /> When thinking about it like that, the notion of something that could qualify as dreaming but is devoid of Glamour would probably be rather suspect to Dream denizens. Can something completely bereft of emotion be considered banal?<br /> <br /> If at some point in the future AI evolves enough to be self-aware, have emotions and all the good stuff, things may change but this is ways off.<br /> <br /> Inanimae sound like a really interesting concept, I've noticed it in discussions before. Before I dive into that it looks like I would need to get the core book and have a crash course though, to have a chance to understand what is going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end the name is quite misleading. You can find literal dreams happening at the Dreaming, and you may decide for your chronicle that it <b>is</b> indeed the realm of dreams, but considering how the Dreaming works in CtD it actually doesn't works so well like that. It isn't Maya, it isn't a part of the Dream Zone, and most dreams probably can't be accessed from there unless something makes them manifest there. Given how it works, someone <i>seeking</i> a dream-space there could cause the Dreaming itself to reach the Dream Zone and manifest the dream-space there, but that wouldn't be the same as them naturally happening there.<br /> <br /> Now, saying what causes Glamour is complicated. We have things like the Inanimae and also Glades, Freehold-like sources of Glamour that exist in wild places without contact to humans. Other than that, human-related Glamour, and as such connection to the Dreaming, tends to occur where people share inspiration instead of around the things that inspire them. <u>If lots of children share stories about a haunted mansion around a campfire, the Glamour doesn't take form in the haunted mansion, but around the campfire</u>, even if the result may be a version of the mansion appearing at its location in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Banality is not just the lack of imagination, it is the crushing of it. Do not think of it as an absence. Something may be fueled with both Glamour and Banality, by the way, or just don't have much of either. They're antagonistic, but not conceptual opposites. DeepDream by itself would probably be considered a wonderful thing by the fae. Its lack of feeling is irrelevant in comparison to how its work inspires and exists just for the sake of sparking imagination. A face-recognition software used give funny labels to people in photos wouldn't be a thing of Banality, but one used to erase jokes and nicknames and enforce proper identification for the sake of sobriety would be Banal.<br /> <br /> You should also understand the psychology of denizens of the Dreaming. They're the most likely splat to embrace any kind of new idea, adventure, curiosity, and throw caution through the window. Excessive caution is Banal, as is fear that paralyzes instead of fueling story. Whatever comes from such new phenomena, they'll hate or love, they'll try to conquer or ally with, they'll interact and spread tales about instead of just avoiding. Even their cautionary tales have always a note of daring instead of simply saying you shouldn't try something. They're bonkers, really. Also, they already have tales about meeting, befriending, vowing revenge on things like seasons, mountains, the concept of social class, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T18:17:51-07:00","id":1490834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep#post1490718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I never played CtD, but have some basic understanding of the Dreaming from crossing over from other splats. My current campaign has an oneiromancer, and I had an idea for something I might need some pointers for from players / STs with a little more direct experience.<br /> <br /> Google <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepDream&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">DeepDream</a> was a project that (initially) explored the possibility of taking a look inside the black box of a neural network, which is usually something very difficult to do. They side-stepped the issue by using a network trained on image recognition and made it 'run in reverse' - I won't get into software engineering details on how that is misleading, but it suffices as a generalization.<br /> <br /> Machine Learning software has become very prominent since then; things like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Dungeon&amp;quot;]AI</a> Dungeon[/URL] popped up, and currently image creators like <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://openai.com/blog/dall-e/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">DALL-E</a> or <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.midjourney.com/showcase/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Midjourney</a> are vogue. Commercially, Machine Learning algorithms are pretty widespread for anything that involves pattern recognition, like search and recommendation engines, the visual processing of self-driving cars, surveillance and so on.<br /> <br /> I'm avoiding calling them Artificial Intelligence because while results get more impressive, they are still a far cry from conscious. Within the WoD however, true AI already exists.<br /> <br /> My point here is, could the current state of rudimentary 'creativity' of ML together with the widespread application of the technology already be enough to affect the Dreaming? Could you imagine a 'section' of the Dreaming where those created images and stories accumulate to build a new realm? Or would it be its own thing, a Chimare separate from the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> Extrapolating from this, would the created Chimeras be different from those created by human dreamers? It's difficult not to project <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://futurism.com/ai-nightmare-crungus&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">expectations</a> into those images, even though the neural net that created them has no idea what the images represent.<br /> <br /> Is there any official release that explores machine dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Im being ironic and not disrespectful: read it as a sort of &quot;half-in-character&quot; quotation*<br /> <br /> All I've heard you saying was Bla Bla Bla Banality, Banality, and more Banality.<br /> <br /> Changelling the Dreaming is like the &quot;make-believe&quot; children play... If those were real!<br /> <br /> AIs that use (urgh, disgusting) &quot;science&quot; are the most banality ridden things imaginable.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is imagination, creativity and fantasy; hard coded and <i>boring</i> &quot;Science&quot; (even if it's the fantastical kind done by the Technocrats) is absolutely anathema to the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> An AI COULD perhaps &quot;Dream&quot;, but it would need to have some sort of &quot;true soul&quot;, whatever that could mean for your WoD games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T18:28:04-07:00","id":1490835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490728#post1490728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The upcoming lore of the traditions explains that the notion of the digital web is not necessarily as limited as previous editions have presented it as. In particular, the author of the chapter on the virtual Adepts is on record saying that in his view, every Mage potentially has access to some aspect of the digital web; and the other aspects aren't necessarily digital. There is mention of a verbena style part of the digital web that has a very organic aspect to it. And I'm sure that there are some steampunk enthusiasts who access a more mechanical portion of the digital web, something with much more of a steampunk aesthetic. I mentioned the latter because to the extent that changeling deals with technology, it typically deals with it in terms of a steampunk aesthetic.<br /> <br /> But I get what you're saying. I will also note that there is a cyber web in the middle umbra which serves as a bridge of sorts between the Middle umbra and the digital web. It would not surprise me in the least if there was something similar in the dreaming. As I said, though, the Dreaming version is more likely to have Steampunk aesthetics, with gears and clockwork automatons rather than electricity. Possibly play up how the originals Difference Engine was inspired by automated looms, and present stored data in the form of elaborate tapestries.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the point of calling it the <b>Digital</b> Web if it's just another middle umbra then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T19:05:34-07:00","id":1490836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490798#post1490798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. The C20 Core isn't a bad initiation, but their original sourcebook will help a lot. The Wiki does it too, if this is not an option (for some reason the people that update the Changeling pages in the wiki has the tendency to fully parse the original text, btw).<br /> <br /> <br /> At the end the name is quite misleading. You can find literal dreams happening at the Dreaming, and you may decide for your chronicle that it <b>is</b> indeed the realm of dreams, but considering how the Dreaming works in CtD it actually doesn't works so well like that. It isn't Maya, it isn't a part of the Dream Zone, and most dreams probably can't be accessed from there unless something makes them manifest there. Given how it works, someone <i>seeking</i> a dream-space there could cause the Dreaming itself to reach the Dream Zone and manifest the dream-space there, but that wouldn't be the same as them naturally happening there.<br /> <br /> Now, saying what causes Glamour is complicated. We have things like the Inanimae and also Glades, Freehold-like sources of Glamour that exist in wild places without contact to humans. Other than that, human-related Glamour, and as such connection to the Dreaming, tends to occur where people share inspiration instead of around the things that inspire them. <u>If lots of children share stories about a haunted mansion around a campfire, the Glamour doesn't take form in the haunted mansion, but around the campfire</u>, even if the result may be a version of the mansion appearing at its location in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Banality is not just the lack of imagination, it is the crushing of it. Do not think of it as an absence. Something may be fueled with both Glamour and Banality, by the way, or just don't have much of either. They're antagonistic, but not conceptual opposites. DeepDream by itself would probably be considered a wonderful thing by the fae. Its lack of feeling is irrelevant in comparison to how its work inspires and exists just for the sake of sparking imagination. A face-recognition software used give funny labels to people in photos wouldn't be a thing of Banality, but one used to erase jokes and nicknames and enforce proper identification for the sake of sobriety would be Banal.<br /> <br /> You should also understand the psychology of denizens of the Dreaming. They're the most likely splat to embrace any kind of new idea, adventure, curiosity, and throw caution through the window. Excessive caution is Banal, as is fear that paralyzes instead of fueling story. Whatever comes from such new phenomena, they'll hate or love, they'll try to conquer or ally with, they'll interact and spread tales about instead of just avoiding. Even their cautionary tales have always a note of daring instead of simply saying you shouldn't try something. They're bonkers, really. Also, they already have tales about meeting, befriending, vowing revenge on things like seasons, mountains, the concept of social class, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe looking into Dark Ages Fae may help give a hint on the origins of &quot;Glamour&quot;. DA Fae had the &quot;Mists&quot; - which may be hard to define, but in WtA terms it could be called perhaps the Wyld? And in MtA, perhaps it's Quintessence? Anyway, The Mists is the primordial source of magic, whatever that means. In DA Fae, there are 3 basic origins for the Fae, the Firstborn, the Inanime and the Changellings.<br /> <br /> Changellings in DA Fae could be called as &quot;half-fae&quot;. They occur when a Fae has... Well, intercourse with a human. But not only that; the children of a changelling is always a changelling too. But, when a Fae kidnaps a human baby and switches him with a Fae baby, both become changellings too, no matter who the Fae parents were. And, kidnapped humans that remain in the Fae realms for too long, become changellings too. Changellings are the lowest &quot;caste&quot; of Fae.<br /> <br /> The Inanime are those who have Inanime parents, but they can also occur &quot;naturally&quot;, probably from the interaction of the Mists with matter. So, it's basically the &quot;magic energy&quot; turning crude matter alive.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Firstborn can just be the children of Firstborn parents, obviously, but their other origin is being born directly from the Mists. Thus the designation &quot;Firstborn&quot; and thus being beings of pure magic. Which is why they are considered the highest caste among Fae society.<br /> <br /> Thus, DA Fae gives authority to the idea that the Fae are probably born from the &quot;primordial dreams&quot;. My theory (headcannon) is that the Dreaming is the &quot;primordial dream of creation&quot;. When the Tellurian was being born/created, it began first in dreams - or the dreams of the first things created sprung the Dreaming/Mists.<br /> <br /> Or, the Dreaming could be &quot;The One&quot; (God)'s dreams of creation - poetically akin to hinduism, upon which the entire Universe is part of Vishnu's (the creator) dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T19:36:54-07:00","id":1490839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490834#post1490834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Im being ironic and not disrespectful: read it as a sort of &quot;half-in-character&quot; quotation*<br /> <br /> All I've heard you saying was Bla Bla Bla Banality, Banality, and more Banality.<br /> <br /> Changelling the Dreaming is like the &quot;make-believe&quot; children play... If those were real!<br /> <br /> AIs that use (urgh, disgusting) &quot;science&quot; are the most banality ridden things imaginable.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is imagination, creativity and fantasy; hard coded and <i>boring</i> &quot;Science&quot; (even if it's the fantastical kind done by the Technocrats) is absolutely anathema to the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> An AI COULD perhaps &quot;Dream&quot;, but it would need to have some sort of &quot;true soul&quot;, whatever that could mean for your WoD games</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is less this being irony and more it being wrong.<br /> <br /> Science isn't disgusting in any sense, shape or form to the Fae, and many a Chimera are based on science fiction of all sorts. Knockers in particular are likely to find this opinion offensive and be quite colorful in their words about that, and some nobles from House Dougal would swear allegiance to the Union for an opportunity to go to Autochtonia. Granted, this opinion is possibly popular among the Pooka (not all, and my current game has even a PC Pooka that became a Dougal Esquire).<br /> <br /> Changelings have nothing against science, even hard science, as long as it furthers imagination (as Julius Verne books do). It is not about proposing the impossible, it is about finding adventure and wonder. The reason why Technocrats are usually regarded as high Banality,,, is actually just that this is kind of their trope in the WoD, roughly justified in their dedication to make the world more mundane. It must be said that they only started to stir out of this stereotype almost at the end of 2nd edition, so all CtD books had already been published (<i>Revised</i> didn't touched it AFAIK).<br /> <br /> Also, do not take DA: Fae at face value. It is among the DA books that most ignored its modern material, and it is still in the air if it's really canon. Not a bad book, that's not the point, but it does have a lot of problems connecting to CtD canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T19:51:26-07:00","id":1490840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490839#post1490839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is less this being irony and more it being wrong.<br /> <br /> Science isn't disgusting in any sense, shape or form to the Fae, and many a Chimera are based on science fiction of all sorts. Knockers in particular are likely to find this opinion offensive and be quite colorful in their words about that, and some nobles from House Dougal would swear allegiance to the Union for an opportunity to go to Autochtonia. Granted, this opinion is possibly popular among the Pooka (not all, and my current game has even a PC Pooka that became a Dougal Esquire).<br /> <br /> Changelings have nothing against science, even hard science, as long as it furthers imagination (as Julius Verne books do). It is not about proposing the impossible, it is about finding adventure and wonder. The reason why Technocrats are usually regarded as high Banality,,, is actually just that this is kind of their trope in the WoD, roughly justified in their dedication to make the world more mundane. It must be said that they only started to stir out of this stereotype almost at the end of 2nd edition, so all CtD books had already been published (<i>Revised</i> didn't touched it AFAIK).<br /> <br /> Also, do not take DA: Fae at face value. It is among the DA books that most ignored its modern material, and it is still in the air if it's really canon. Not a bad book, that's not the point, but it does have a lot of problems connecting to CtD canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Im super sleepy right now and super lazy for it. Indeed, science fiction is super glamour-ish. And the wonders of science are too.<br /> <br /> Modern AIs that create &quot;art&quot; thou are super banal. They stifle creativity like nothing else. So much so that people are already asking themselves if &quot;artists will lose their jobs&quot;. I cant imagine a heavier blow to the Dreaming than this - masses of dreamers actively GIVING UP on their ability to &quot;dream&quot; because they are being replaced by souless and emotionless machines. &quot;What's the point of trying to make a song or paint a painting if nobody wants to buy my work because &quot;DeepGoogle&quot; is so much better at it? I wont even try&quot;.<br /> <br /> That to me would be the final blown delivered by the autumn people, and the final winter to all Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T02:32:49-07:00","id":1490855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490798#post1490798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end the name is quite misleading. You can find literal dreams happening at the Dreaming, and you may decide for your chronicle that it <b>is</b> indeed the realm of dreams, but considering how the Dreaming works in CtD it actually doesn't works so well like that. It isn't Maya, it isn't a part of the Dream Zone, and most dreams probably can't be accessed from there unless something makes them manifest there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really doesn't help that MtA and WtA books use the names interchangeably and directly state 'this is where dreams and dreamers go at night'. I guess I fell victim to the biased POV of the splats. Fair enough, but it's annoying that I have to unlearn this now if I want to add more CtD elements consistently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490798#post1490798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, saying what causes Glamour is complicated. We have things like the Inanimae and also Glades, Freehold-like sources of Glamour that exist in wild places without contact to humans. Other than that, human-related Glamour, and as such connection to the Dreaming, tends to occur where people share inspiration instead of around the things that inspire them. <u>If lots of children share stories about a haunted mansion around a campfire, the Glamour doesn't take form in the haunted mansion, but around the campfire</u>, even if the result may be a version of the mansion appearing at its location in the Near Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanical question here is whether or not Glamour is needed to shape the animate and inanimate Chimera that make up the dream landscape of the mansion. As a somewhat silly example, I could prompt one of the image creating neural nets to create a picture of the mansion which then 'dreams up' the result, and then I close the browser tab before even looking at it. I don't think this would produce a 'true' dream-space of the mansion, because there was no wonder involved anywhere in the creation process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490836#post1490836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe looking into Dark Ages Fae may help give a hint on the origins of &quot;Glamour&quot;. DA Fae had the &quot;Mists&quot; - which may be hard to define, but in WtA terms it could be called perhaps the Wyld? And in MtA, perhaps it's Quintessence? Anyway, The Mists is the primordial source of magic, whatever that means. In DA Fae, there are 3 basic origins for the Fae, the Firstborn, the Inanime and the Changellings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a lot like the Wyld in Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490840#post1490840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern AIs that create &quot;art&quot; thou are super banal. They stifle creativity like nothing else. So much so that people are already asking themselves if &quot;artists will lose their jobs&quot;. I cant imagine a heavier blow to the Dreaming than this - masses of dreamers actively GIVING UP on their ability to &quot;dream&quot; because they are being replaced by souless and emotionless machines. &quot;What's the point of trying to make a song or paint a painting if nobody wants to buy my work because &quot;DeepGoogle&quot; is so much better at it? I wont even try&quot;.<br /> <br /> That to me would be the final blown delivered by the autumn people, and the final winter to all Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the artist communities I frequent, this is mostly an assumed attitude from an outside perspective. The vast majority of artists I know see ML generated content for what it is: a new tool that can help the creative process. There are some who use it as inspiration or template for their own art. Others use assets created by it, and others again shift the creative process into finding the correct prompts to create the desired result.<br /> If anything, visual ML engines have increased the speed of the process and opened it to a whole bunch of people who previously did not even engage in visual arts. The same already happened before with digital painting (vs traditional methods) or digital audio workstations for music, including fears it would trivialize the respective art.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:01:03-07:00","id":1490870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490835#post1490835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the point of calling it the <b>Digital</b> Web if it's just another middle umbra then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said that the Digital Web is just another Middle Umbra? Fundamentally, the Digital Web is (part of) a Realm of mathematical truth, the connection between the Correspondence Point and the rest of reality. You don't need to be digital to be about the primacy of information, though; both the Ahl-i-Batin with their Mount Qaf and the Akashayana with their Akashic Record have demonstrated this. The fact that the Verbena have also figured out how to use biology (specifically DNA) for programming just points to another sector of the broader information hypersphere that the Digital Web turns out to just be one part of. (I would also point you to the Platonic Realm as described in the STV product <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/367375\" target=\"_blank\">Paradigm Explored: Number and Shape</a> as a sort of \u201cbridge\u201d between the Astral Umbra and the Hypersphere. It strikes me as the \u201cHermetic beachhead\u201d in what the VAs would call \u201cdigital space\u201d.)<br /> <br /> Though IMHO, using DNA for programming purposes strikes me as more of a Progenitors thing than a Verbena thing. The point remains, though, that computation needn't be a technomantic thing. <br /> <br /> All that said, that's a topic that has much more relevance to the Mage forum than to the Changeling forum. Bringing it (somewhat) back on topic, saying that the Digital Web is \u201cjust another Middle Umbra\u201d is like saying that the <i>Dreaming</i> is \u201cjust another Umbra\u201d. You can point out some broad similarities (e.g., Chimerical Reality is similar to the Penumbra, and the Near and Deep Dreaming are similar to how the Umbra can be divided into regions near the Penumbra and distant from it; one might even call them the Near Umbra and the Deep Umbra). But despite those similarities, that doesn't mean that the Dreaming is in <i>all</i> ways equivalent to the Umbra. It merely has some parallels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-21-2022, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:16:39-07:00","id":1490872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490855#post1490855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really doesn't help that MtA and WtA books use the names interchangeably and directly state 'this is where dreams and dreamers go at night'. I guess I fell victim to the biased POV of the splats. Fair enough, but it's annoying that I have to unlearn this now if I want to add more CtD elements consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that early on, the Maya/Dream Zone and the Dreaming <i>were</i> considered to be the same thing by the authors. It's been a more recent development to say that the Dreaming is distinct from the Dream Zone. My own approach to that is to say that the Dream Zone is kind of like a bridge between the Dreaming and the Umbra, in a manner <i>kind of like</i> how the CyberRealm can sort of be thought of as a bridge between the Digital Web and the Umbra. <br /> <br /> For the purpose of this thread, I think it would be appropriate for there to be some sort of \u201cbridge realm\u201d between the Dreaming and the Digital Web, in much the same way that there are bridge realms between each of them and the Umbra. It would represent something that mathematicians are all too familiar with, but which the general public seems intent on denying even exists: there is imagination and wonder in mathematics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-21-2022, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T12:56:47-07:00","id":1490914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490855#post1490855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanical question here is whether or not Glamour is needed to shape the animate and inanimate Chimera that make up the dream landscape of the mansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Glamour used to shape the mansion comes from the Dreaming itself, and so does the form of the Mansion. Contrary to what happens with the Umbra, the Chimerical Mansion isn't simply a mirror of the beliefs of the people who told or heard the stories. And the Dream Mansion doesn't necessarily have any direct connection to the Mansion, either. If the people that tell stories do so from afar, while the people really around the mansion pays it no attention, it may be even a high Banality place despite being the inspiration to a Dreaming location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490855#post1490855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a somewhat silly example, I could prompt one of the image creating neural nets to create a picture of the mansion which then 'dreams up' the result, and then I close the browser tab before even looking at it. I don't think this would produce a 'true' dream-space of the mansion, because there was no wonder involved anywhere in the creation process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, saying who's really able to wonder or not is hard when it comes to the Dreaming. How's there Glamour in a Glade no sapient being ever saw? I'm not saying that the formation of the mansion would be likely. Not even if you saw it the formation would be likely, as it would still be the imagination of a single person. Yet, the problem is that with the Dreaming you always have a chance of things happening. So while the chance of something happening just with your experiment would be small. <b>But not zero</b>.<br /> <br /> In addition to that, sometimes the Dreaming will have a One-In-A-Million event happening just because that's interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490855#post1490855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds a lot like the Wyld in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably it is. AFAIK DA: Fae is from the time they were trying to establish Exalted as the ancient past of the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490855#post1490855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the artist communities I frequent, this is mostly an assumed attitude from an outside perspective. The vast majority of artists I know see ML generated content for what it is: a new tool that can help the creative process.</div> </div> </div> </div>An artist pressed into producing at a high pace even during a creative block, so it become less an act of imagination as it is an obligation to feed yourself, is far more likely to be highly banal than a machine. And if the machine-produced image made many people day-dream with stories and whatnot, then it did the job.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the extremely elaborate and well made painting created by a professional artist that gave it little thought beyond making it in time may be beautiful to watch, but it has much less Glamour than the doodle of someone completely inept at it, inscribing a mess no one else is capable of making any sense of, but done as their way of expressing love, fear, telling a story they're really excited about, or even done while daydreaming of one day become as good as the first artist.<br /> <br /> Glamour is <b>not</b> about <b>Art</b>, although most artists understand what it is about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490872#post1490872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the issue is that early on, the Maya/Dream Zone and the Dreaming <i>were</i> considered to be the same thing by the authors. It's been a more recent development to say that the Dreaming is distinct from the Dream Zone. My own approach to that is to say that the Dream Zone is kind of like a bridge between the Dreaming and the Umbra, in a manner <i>kind of like</i> how the CyberRealm can sort of be thought of as a bridge between the Digital Web and the Umbra.<br /> <br /> For the purpose of this thread, I think it would be appropriate for there to be some sort of \u201cbridge realm\u201d between the Dreaming and the Digital Web, in much the same way that there are bridge realms between each of them and the Umbra. It would represent something that mathematicians are all too familiar with, but which the general public seems intent on denying even exists: there is imagination and wonder in mathematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the old-fashioned lack of consistency in the setting, as they wanted to reference everything everywhere, but at the same time make every line as independent as possible.<br /> <br /> As a consequence, while the Dreaming was intended to be the Realm of Dreams and all that, it happened that CtD was the line that paid less heed to the rules on the Umbra. As a result, while there are discrepancies in Umbral rules between lines, the Dreaming simply ended up contradicting it too much. And it went far with its own rules and stuff, to the point that <b><i>simply</i></b> conflating it with some Umbral phenomena or the Umbra itself became impossible.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem went unaddressed, unobserved and disregarded for a long time, further complicating things, at least if one is to try and make the Dreaming a part of the Umbra as it was sort-of intended.<br /> <br /> In the end the result isn't bad, it just doesn't work as originally intended. I personally find it far more interesting as it is now, for the purpose it has in the game. But to make a crossover that respects all the lines it simply have to be seen as its own thing, and read about in its native CtD setting, precisely because of this problem: assumptions brought from other lines will miss the mark royally.<br /> <br /> C20 seems to use this premise, as in how it describes some Paths of Balor as leading to this &quot;strange, alien place the Werewolves call 'Umbra'&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:31:09-07:00","id":1490921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490914#post1490914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Glamour used to shape the mansion comes from the Dreaming itself, and so does the form of the Mansion. Contrary to what happens with the Umbra, the Chimerical Mansion isn't simply a mirror of the beliefs of the people who told or heard the stories. And the Dream Mansion doesn't necessarily have any direct connection to the Mansion, either. If the people that tell stories do so from afar, while the people really around the mansion pays it no attention, it may be even a high Banality place despite being the inspiration to a Dreaming location.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, saying who's really able to wonder or not is hard when it comes to the Dreaming. How's there Glamour in a Glade no sapient being ever saw? I'm not saying that the formation of the mansion would be likely. Not even if you saw it the formation would be likely, as it would still be the imagination of a single person. Yet, the problem is that with the Dreaming you always have a chance of things happening. So while the chance of something happening just with your experiment would be small. <b>But not zero</b>.<br /> <br /> In addition to that, sometimes the Dreaming will have a One-In-A-Million event happening just because that's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That very much makes it sound like the Dreaming is a conscious actor. Which I could deal with, some other realms also display something like agency.<br /> Treating the Dreaming, Maya, and the Dream Zone as different things is probably the way to go for me here, although I will have to sort out some possible specific problems from having ST'd things with a flawed understanding. Worst case I'll have just to pull through with my current way, since the players didn't really encounter any CtD related things yet, aside from a few Chimera in personal dreams.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490872#post1490872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purpose of this thread, I think it would be appropriate for there to be some sort of \u201cbridge realm\u201d between the Dreaming and the Digital Web, in much the same way that there are bridge realms between each of them and the Umbra. It would represent something that mathematicians are all too familiar with, but which the general public seems intent on denying even exists: there is imagination and wonder in mathematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I agree with this, describing a Realm that represents the wonder in G\u00f6del's Incompleteness Theorems or the fascination of the Amplituhedron would be a major challenge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-21-2022, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:53:32-07:00","id":1490926,"title":"","content":"I think you can treat the Maya and the Dream Zone as the same thing, and the Dreaming as something distinct but related \u2014 and something that, at one point in the past, may have been less related (see <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T14:12:59-07:00","id":1490928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1490718-electric-sheep?p=1490921#post1490921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That very much makes it sound like the Dreaming is a conscious actor. Which I could deal with, some other realms also display something like agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is heavily implied to either be, or be run by such a complex set of laws as to function as if it was a conscious actor.<br /> <br /> Bridge realms probably can help you with this, and as a &quot;conscious&quot; realm the Dreaming may be able to trickle within or from the Dream Zone to justify discrepancies. For example, if a Dream-Space was sought off by a Changeling in the Dreaming at some point, the realm could cause it to exist both in the Dreaming and the Dream-Zone at the same time, so a Changeling found there would for all purposes be a native (from their perspective, they <b>are</b> in the Dreaming). I'm not sure about the actual discrepancies you have to deal with, but that may help. Also, C20 already have official (if uncommon) ways to reach the Umbra from the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Other than that, do what your chronicle needs. As always, everything said is relevant only from the perspective of analyzing it under the official CtD lore. You'll have a perfectly good baseline assuming the Fae as a somewhat specific class of Wyld spirits and go from there, few mechanical changes would be required. The Dreaming may be the intercession between the Dream-Zone and some part of the Astral Umbra, and there may also be some realm dedicated to Banality, so again it is a spiritual thing that opposes Glamour instead of just being an absence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:40:21-07:00","id":1491024,"title":"","content":"Mount Qaf has a presence in the Deep Dreaming. So the digital web need not be beyond reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:46:05-07:00","id":1491310,"title":"","content":"This has been sizzling in my brain for a while, and I think I made a step forward in constructing a possible Realm. It was still nagging me that the 'stuff' a machine dream realm would be made of would be very different to either Chimera or Emanations. At its fundamental level, it is still emotionless.<br /> <br /> So I decided to build with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entropy_(information_theory)\" target=\"_blank\">Shannon Entropy</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negentropy\" target=\"_blank\">Negentropy</a>. If you read the intro description of the two, you will note some vague similarities to Glamour and Banality in an abstracted way, reduced to informational quality. There are also some inspirational analyses of Shannon Entropy in neural nets I can draw on. I think those are some basic building blocks I can work with, and it touches on the ideas <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> presented here, too. A new and unique type of dreamstuff is also something my player would enjoy to discover and study.<br /> <br /> I think divorcing it from the Dreaming and the usual Realms of the Umbra is the practical way to go. The new Realm (or probably rather budding Zone) would still be connected to either, although I imagine it as something that is still in a very early stage of development. Any connections to other Realms would be very unstable and coincidental.<br /> <br /> For the landscape I have plenty of examples to draw on from the visual ML programs, though I want to make it a look into the 'mind' of those primitive nets and give it a touch of structured chaos, if that makes sense. I'm also figuring out possible encounters; the way I see it, this realm would be very Weaver-ish and Wyld-ish (sorry for the WtA terms) at the same time, so I'm not sure yet what those would be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-25-2022, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}